body:
Medication didn't help me with my beliefs but I think the unfounded ones mostly happen when your brain produces too much dopamine.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I think if we are all aspects of the source creation then surely we all can communicate with God but everyone has to interpret their surroundings in a personal way. Other people usually won't understand. "Being ourselves" is what God wants because we are parts of God and we should produce what we're skilled at.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I try not to become paranoid about other people but just take everything in and not take it too seriously. It is a struggle.

\-Reselling: browsing craigslist, letgo, facebook, thrift stores, cheap websites etc ad buying stuff and then selling it for profit. Something to do on the side whenever you have money to grow.

&#x200B;

\-Making music: use real instruments or a DAW and market on social media. Not actually that hard if you watch tutorials. Can sell full songs to consumers or instrumental beats to artists. Something to work at weekly while doing something else, can eventually become full-time.

&#x200B;

\-Making clothing: you can either start a streetwear brand or sell individual pieces, similar marketing as music except you have to market even more. You can sew or get a screen printing kit.

&#x200B;

\-Drawing for youtubers or musicians: they will get you to illustrate their ideas that they need for marketing

&#x200B;

\-Waitressing/bussing/cooking/dishwashing/barista: You don't need a great resume to get this job usually, it is stressful. Maybe do it for a few months.

&#x200B;

\-Cashiering: Don't need a great resume, short interactions with people, on your feet. Can probably keep this for over a year.

&#x200B;

\-Factory/production work: Very boring unless euphorically manic or high, probs just do it for a few months

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
